    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/279610": {
      "title": "Transfer Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Transfer Admissions Counselor - Traditional Day You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Transfer Admissions Counselor - Traditional Day Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Degree Preferred Category Admissions/Recruiting Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented institution with a focus on career-oriented programs in business, engineering, information technology and computer science, criminal justice, life sciences, human services, and many other concentrations. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus and nearly 5,000 students in its College of Professional Studies programs online and onsite at 15 regional locations. Degrees are offered at the associate, bachelor, master, and doctoral levels. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Institute of Technology embraces diversity and equal opportunity intentionally. We are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that diversity and inclusion among our employees is critical to our success with respect to educating our students to become global citizens. Indiana Tech is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan . Reporting to the Executive Director of Admissions, the Transfer Admissions Counselor is responsible for recruiting, counseling, and enrolling prospective transfer students into Indiana Tech’s traditional undergraduate programs. This position serves as the primary point of contact for transfer students throughout the admissions process, including application review, transfer credit evaluation coordination, financial aid guidance, and enrollment advising. The Transfer Admissions Counselor develops and maintains relationships with community colleges, faculty, staff, and external partners to facilitate transfer pathways and increase transfer student enrollment. The position works collaboratively with the Transfer Advisor in the Office of Student Success and other campus partners to support a seamless transition from admission through enrollment, promote student success, and enhance the overall transfer student experience. Work will be performed in a manner that contributes to the university’s enrollment objectives while supporting Indiana Tech’s mission, vision, and values. The Transfer Admissions Counselor serves as an active member of the Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force and collaborates across campus to improve transfer processes, strengthen partnerships, and advance initiatives that support transfer student recruitment, enrollment, and success. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Transfer Recruitment and Enrollment Recruit prospective transfer students through in-person appointments, phone calls, text messaging, email communications, virtual meetings, and admissions events. Manage transfer recruitment and develop strategies to increase transfer student enrollment. Build and maintain relationships with community colleges, academic advisors, faculty, and transfer coordinators. Represent Indiana Tech at transfer fairs, community college visits, campus events, and other recruitment activities. Assist transfer students through the admissions, financial aid, and enrollment processes. Conduct individual counseling sessions with students regarding transfer opportunities, degree programs, costs, and scholarship options. Develop and execute transfer-specific communication and recruitment plans designed to generate applications, deposits, and enrollments. Transfer Credit Evaluation and Admissions Review Request, monitor, and coordinate transfer credit evaluations with the Transfer Advisor and other campus partners. Review completed transfer evaluations with students and explain degree applicability, remaining requirements, and graduation pathways. Conduct preliminary reviews of transcripts and admissions documents to determine admissions eligibility and application readiness. Make admissions recommendations and decisions in accordance with institutional policies and established admission standards. Advocate for students to maximize transferability of previously earned coursework. Complete transcript reviews, transfer credit evaluations, admissions evaluations, application processing, and other enrollment-related duties as needed during peak application and enrollment periods. Student Success Collaboration Collaborate closely with the Transfer Advisor in the Office of Student Success to support a seamless transition for transfer students from admission through enrollment and persistence. Coordinate regularly regarding transfer student needs, academic planning, registration readiness, and student support services. Partner with the Transfer Advisor to identify and address barriers to enrollment, retention, and student success. Participate in joint outreach efforts and initiatives designed to improve the transfer student experience and increase student persistence. Share relevant student information and enrollment updates in accordance with institutional policies to ensure continuity of support throughout the student lifecycle. Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force Serve as an active member of the Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force. Collaborate with campus partners to identify opportunities to improve transfer student recruitment, enrollment, retention, and graduation outcomes. Assist in the development and implementation of transfer initiatives, articulation agreements, policies, and procedures. Provide feedback and recommendations based on transfer student trends, challenges, and enrollment data. Support institutional efforts to create and enhance transfer pathways that improve student access and success. Team Collaboration and Operational Support Participate in admissions events including visit programs, open houses, accepted student events, orientation activities, and transfer-specific programs. Assist with recruitment travel, presentations, and outreach initiatives as assigned. Support departmental recruitment initiatives and collaborate with admissions staff to ensure enrollment goals are achieved. Contribute to a positive team environment and assist with special projects and additional responsibilities as assigned. Adhere to all university, state, and federal regulations related to student recruitment and admissions practices. Measures of Accomplishment Achievement of individual and departmental transfer enrollment goals. Growth in transfer applications, admits, deposits, and enrolled students. Timely completion of transfer credit evaluations and admissions decisions. Development and maintenance of community college partnerships and transfer pathways. Effective participation and contribution to the Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force. Accurate and timely documentation of student interactions within Slate CRM. Positive service and responsiveness to students, families, and campus partners. Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to travel and maintain insurability under university requirements. Preferred Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and Slate CRM, preferred. Previous experience in admissions, higher education, recruitment, sales, customer service, or transfer student services, preferred. Familiarity with transfer credit evaluation processes, articulation agreements, and student success initiatives, preferred. Experience Two years or more work experience within admissions is preferred, and bachelor’s degree required. Application materials must include a cover letter and resume. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/279124": {
      "title": "Financial Systems Accountant",
      "description": "Financial Systems Accountant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Financial Systems Accountant Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Category Accounting Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan . Indiana Tech is seeking a forward-thinking Financial Systems Accountant to join our finance team on the Fort Wayne campus. The Financial Systems Accountant combines expertise in accounting, financial reporting, data analytics, and technology to support and enhance the university's financial operations. This position works closely with other university departments, leadership, and external vendors to ensure financial systems accurately support accounting transactions, financial processes, financial reporting, internal controls, and data governance. The position is responsible for maintaining and optimizing financial applications/systems, developing automated reports and dashboards, improving business processes through technology solutions, and ensuring the integrity and reliability of financial data across multiple systems. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Accounting, Financial Reporting & Data Analytics Perform and support month-end and year-end close processes, including journal entries, reconciliations, and variance analysis. Prepare and analyze monthly and annual financial statements in accordance with GAAP and regulatory standards. Review financial data for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with accounting standards and university policies. Perform balance sheet account reconciliations and investigate discrepancies Assists with budgeting and forecasting processes. Support audit requests by providing documentation, data analyses, and system process information. Provide financial data for external surveys and reports. Develop and maintain dashboards and reports that support cash management, accounts receivable, accounts payable, fixed assets, and general ledger activities and monitor financial performance and KPIs. Analyze large datasets to identify trends, anomalies, and opportunities for cost savings or revenue enhancement. Maintain internal database files and tables and develop custom reports/queries to meet the needs of the finance department and university leadership. Collaborate with departments to ensure accurate financial coding and reporting. Monitor system processes that impact accounting transactions and recommend improvements when issues are identified. Ensure financial system configurations support proper accounting treatment and reporting requirements. Systems Administration & Automation Serve as a subject matter expert and collaborate with university departments to integrate and automate financial systems. Manage internal and external system upgrades, integrations, configurations, user permissions, and data integrity across platforms. Ensure systems comply with financial regulations and internal controls. Monitor system performance and conduct regular audits. Troubleshoot system issues and work with IT, university departments, and vendors to resolve problems. Participate in system and process re-engineering efforts and automation. Process Improvement & Optimization Identify opportunities to streamline financial processes and workflows to enhance accuracy, efficiency, and scalability. Develop reconciliation processes to ensure reporting consistency. Utilize tools such as Power Query, Power BI, Power Automate, Vena, and other technologies to improve operational efficiency. Conduct assessment of software and hardware needs and design new or modified systems to meet changing demands. Evaluate the impact of changes and recommend enhancements. Maintain documentation of procedures and develop training materials for system users and finance staff. Provide training and support to finance staff and departmental users on system functionality and best practices. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field. Advanced proficiency in Excel and experience with data visualization tools (e.g., Power BI, Power Query, pivot tables, lookups). Hands-on experience and knowledge with ERP, financial reporting, and automation platforms or AI agents (e.g., Jenzabar, Vena, Supervity, Microsoft 365). Broad knowledge of techniques in collecting data, analyzing information, generating reports,  or other data querying languages. Innovative with an eagerness to learn new processes and naturally curious. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills with intense attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Knowledge of financial internal controls and compliance frameworks. Self-starter and ability to work within a team, independently, and collaboratively across the university Experience 5+ years of progressive accounting experience, with at least 2-3 years in a data or systems-focused role. Working Conditions Work is typically performed in a standard office environment on university premises, with occasional travel. Some evening and weekend work may be required and/or necessary. Physical presence on campus during scheduled working hours is an essential function of this position. The employee must be able to consistently report to work on university premises, participate in in-person and remote meetings and activities, and perform duties requiring on-site access to university facilities, systems, records, and resources. Application materials must include a cover letter and resume. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/279058": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - COE - Computer Engineering In-Person You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - COE - Computer Engineering In-Person Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Preferred Category Education Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking a knowledgeable and experienced Adjunct Faculty Member to join our online engineering program. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in engineering, a passion for teaching, and the ability to engage and inspire students in a virtual learning environment . Essential Duties & Responsibilities Teaching courses as needed. Maintain academic records of courses to assist in specialized accreditation. Collaborate with other degree programs on campus outside of computer engineering. Support efforts to increase access and success in higher education for underrepresented populations. Support the mission, vision, and strategic plan of Indiana Institute of Technology. Qualifications A minimum of a Master degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or closely related field is required. College-level teaching experience required. Demonstrated ability to work with a diverse student population. Demonstrated evidence of strong written and oral communication. Experience with a Learning Management System. Applicants should be able to use technology effectively in all aspects of their work, including teaching. Working Conditions Work is normally performed in a typical classroom/office environment and synchronous or asynchronous online environment.  Scheduling must be flexible to accommodate early morning, evening. **The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
